1. THE AGE MOMENT OF A MOVING SOURCE: kappa R_ret against sqrt(x_par^2 + (1 - beta^2) x_perp^2)
  1000 random points and speeds: the identity holds to 2.3e-15; the age moment A = q dwell / (4 pi c kappa R_ret)
  has the level sets x_par^2 + (1 - beta^2) x_perp^2 = const, ellipsoids contracted along the motion by sqrt(1 - beta^2);
  the presence P = q dwell / (4 pi kappa R_ret^2) has not (kappa R_ret^2 is no quadric).

2. THE EXCHANGE BETWEEN CO-MOVING BODIES, THE CONTINUUM LIMIT (rows received per interval over the rest rate)
  beta | forward, no aberration (1-b)^2 | backward (1+b)^2 | transverse (1-b^2) | Galilean aberration: forward | backward | transverse (J (1-b^2)) | classical E: longitudinal (1-b^2) | transverse 1/gamma | transverse drag component beta
  0.2148 | 0.617 | 1.476 | 0.954 | 0.910 | 0.910 | 1.023 | 0.954 | 0.977 | 0.215
  0.4297 | 0.325 | 2.044 | 0.815 | 0.665 | 0.665 | 1.083 | 0.815 | 0.903 | 0.430
  the round trips of the exchange (transit forward + back, over the rest 2 d / c): longitudinal d/(c-v) + d/(c+v) = gamma^2 x rest, transverse 2 gamma d / c = gamma x rest, with or without aberration;
    beta 0.2148: gamma 1.024, gamma^2 1.048
    beta 0.4297: gamma 1.107, gamma^2 1.226

